In the patchlevel9 game I'm currently playing, I'm on dlevel 20.  It's a bones
level, and I didn't take too close a look at what was in the pile, just
glanced at it and went to map the level.  The Olog-hai I'd been beating
back every so often appears next to me suddenly, and "the black blade draws
life....Goodbye level 13"!!
     Luckily I'm invisible and I dodge over to the far corner of the room.
No missile weapons, fireball spell which I'm not sure I can cast...so I
decide on wand of polymorph.  When he shows his face again, I zap him.
Black dragon.  Great, they can't carry weapons, and I finish it off, no
problem.
     When I searched the *whole* area, Stormbringer was nowhere to be found,
only a cursed wide sword where the dragon dropped.  This must be it,
so why isn't it identified as Stormbringer?  I assume the Olog-hai picked
it up from the bones pile I passed over, since he didn't have it before,
but I don't remember seeing "Stormbringer" stick out when I scanned it.
There was another Stormbringer on an earlier bones level, *identified* as
such, and I didn't bring it along (already had a +6 mace and Excalibur).
     That could be the start of an explanation.
I dimly remember some discussion from a while back about what happens when
there's more than one of the same named weapon in the same game.  There
can't exist more than one of the god-given weapons, so the second one loses
its special attacks and becomes just a better-than-average weapon of
its generic type?  But then why did I *lose a level* from a wide sword??

